    "description": "Vintage Estate Tobacco Pipes\nBriar Smoking Pipe Collection\n9 Items, Mid to Late 20th Century\nThis estate lot includes nine vintage briar tobacco smoking pipes presenting a diverse selection of classic English and American shapes, finishes, and makers. The collection features smooth, carved, rusticated, and sandblast bowls across various traditional silhouettes including straight billiards, bent apples, bulldogs, and unique carved freehand forms.\nITEMS INCLUDED:\n1.\nShamrock Briar Pipe\n- Stamped \"SHAMROCK\" on shank with banded ferrule and P-lip style vulcanite stem\n2.\nThe Tinder Box Carved Bent Pipe\n- Stamped \"THE TINDER BOX\" with rusticated and carved bowl styling\n3.\nGolden Grain Bulldog Pipe\n- Stamped \"GOLDEN GRAIN\" on shank, smooth finish with accent ring\n4.\nSenator Bent Apple Pipe\n- Stamped \"SENATOR\" on shank, smooth walnut-tone briar with curved stem\n5.\nGolden Square London Made Pipe\n- Stamped \"GOLDEN SQUARE LONDON MADE\" on shank with stem logo\n6.\nHand Tooled Rhodesian Pipe\n- Stamped \"HAND TOOLED\" on shank, smooth finish with double rim grooving\n7.\nCarved Fluted Panel Pipe\n- Freehand style with deep carved vertical fluting and black stem\n8.\nScot Rusticated Billiard Pipe\n- Dark sandblast/rusticated finish, stem stamped \"SCOT\"\n9.\nScotsman's Delight Billiard Pipe\n- Black rusticated bowl stamped \"SCOTSMAN'S DELIGHT MADE IN ENGLAND\"\nCondition:\nPre-owned vintage estate condition. Bowls show carbon cake and charring consistent with prior use. Stems exhibit varying degrees of oxidation, tooth chatter, and cosmetic wear. All tenons and stems fit securely into shanks with no breaks visible.\nPlease Note:\nThis is a pre-owned item being sold\nas-is\n. We do our best to describe items accurately and include research where possible, but we are not experts in every category. Please note that if the title or description states \"Tested\" that we only test to make sure the unit \"\nPOWERS ON\"\n.\nNo further testing takes place unless stated otherwise and items are considered untested.\nPlease remember all items are used and are sold as is, no refunds.If you have questions, please contact us before bidding.\nFor all vintage clothing, please research sizing before placing a bid.\nItems from different time periods may have measurements that differ from today’s standard sizing.\nCustomer Service:\nReach us via the “Contact Us” link above or by calling\n(540) 361-6550\n. Messages are handled Monday–Friday, 8:00 AM–4:00 PM ET, and we strive to respond within 48 hours.",
